function method(){const a=data.audit;$('methodContent').innerHTML=`<div class="audit-grid"><div><strong>${num(a.eligiblePlays)}</strong><span>ELIGIBLE DROPBACKS</span></div><div><strong>${num(a.scoutingRows)}</strong><span>PLAYER SCOUTING RECORDS</span></div><div><strong>${num(a.trackingRows)}</strong><span>TRACKING OBSERVATIONS</span></div></div><h3>The sample</h3><p>All 32 teams, ${a.games} games, Weeks 1–8 of the 2021 season. This is a historical sample of passing situations, not every offensive snap or a current scouting report. ${num(a.rawPlays)} original plays → ${num(a.eligiblePlays)} eligible plays; ${a.excludedPlays} excluded for a recorded penalty, “No Play” description or two-point attempt. Filters apply before every brief metric.</p><h3>Three measures, three denominators</h3><ul><li><b>Pressure sources:</b> unique player-play pass-rush reps with at least one PFF hit, hurry or sack credit, divided by that player’s pass-rush reps. Players are ordered by credited reps, not a talent ranking. Multiple credits on one rep count once; multiple players can earn credit on one play.</li><li><b>Team pressure:</b> any credited player on a play, counted once, divided by eligible dropbacks. Pressure allowed is a separate PFF label. ${stats.noAllowed} of ${stats.pressure} pressured plays in the current split have no charged blocker.</li><li><b>5+ rushers:</b> five or more unique players with PFF “Pass rush” role, divided by eligible dropbacks. This does not identify simulated pressure or all scheme-defined blitzes. Pressure comparisons use the four-rusher and five-plus-rusher groups’ own denominators.</li><li><b>Coverage:</b> PFF scheme labels divided by plays with a known coverage label. Unknown labels are excluded from that denominator and reported. These are observed outcomes of the call, not a pre-snap recognition model.</li></ul><h3>What the replay can tell you</h3><p>Coordinates are observed, rounded to 0.01 yard, and rotated 180° for left-moving offenses so the offense always moves right. Rush paths follow PFF pass rushers. The QB trail and straight-line displacement from the snap show pocket movement; they do not measure protection quality.</p><p>Frame differences at <a href="https://operations.nfl.com/gameday/technology/nfl-next-gen-stats" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">10 samples per second</a> determine timing because this source’s timestamps have only whole-second precision. The recorded ball_snap takes precedence over the automatic snap tag. Release and sack times require their corresponding event tags; no pressure-onset time is inferred. Replays stop at the last supplied frame. There is no extrapolation beyond the tracking window.</p><p>The usual window starts shortly before the snap and ends shortly after the throw. Full-route, catch-point, after-catch and complete pre-snap motion analysis are not reliably supported. A sack outcome does not guarantee a sack event in the tracking window. The orange ring marks the selected defender to watch. It is a viewing aid, not a pressure-onset marker. The initial selection prefers a sack, hit or hurry credit, then credited volume in the filtered brief; without pressure credits, it selects a pass rusher. White squares identify PFF Pass Block roles, and the gold diamond identifies the quarterback. Hover over a player for the role and exact pressure credit.</p><h3>Validation anchors</h3><div class="validation-list"><span>Cleveland pressure: <b>${a.cleveland.pressure} / ${a.cleveland.n} (${percentage(a.cleveland.pressure,a.cleveland.n)})</b></span><span>Garrett pressure reps: <b>${a.garrett.pressure} / ${a.garrett.reps} (${percentage(a.garrett.pressure,a.garrett.reps)})</b></span><span>Replays: <b>${num(a.playsWithTracking)} / ${num(a.eligiblePlays)}</b></span><span>Eligible plays without a snap tag: <b>${a.playsWithoutSnap}</b></span></div><h3>Reproducible source</h3><p>Scouting: Pro Football Focus. Tracking: NFL Next Gen Stats. Retrieved from the public <a href="${a.source}" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Big Data Bowl regional event repository</a>, pinned to revision <code>${a.revision}</code>. <a href="data/audit.json" target="_blank">Open the machine-readable validation audit</a> for counts and source file hashes.</p><div class="source-missing"><p><b>Missing original inputs:</b> the referenced report.md, opportunity_map.png and example_play.png at /workspace/nfl-analysis were unavailable in this environment. This demo independently rebuilds the metrics and replays from the public CSVs. It does not claim to reproduce the missing report’s full methodology or images.</p></div><h3>Use as a review prompt</h3><p>Small splits below 30 plays are flagged. Rates are descriptive associations with no causal interpretation. Pressure groups include sacks, which directly reduce recorded yardage. Do not infer an assignment, intended QB read, individual blocker failure or coaching prescription from a tracking path alone.</p>`;$('methodDialog').showModal();}
function exportPlays(){const header=['gameId','playId','week','defense','offense','down','yardsToGo','outcome','yards','rushers','pressureCredit','coverage','description'];const rows=visible.map(p=>[p.game,p.play,p.week,p.defense,p.offense,p.down,p.distance,RESULT[p.result],p.yards,p.rushers.length,p.pressure.map(playerName).join('; '),p.coverage,p.description]);const cell=x=>`"${String(x??'').replaceAll('"','""')}"`;const csv=[header,...rows].map(r=>r.map(cell).join(',')).join('\r\n');const u=URL.createObjectURL(new Blob([csv],{type:'text/csv;charset=utf-8'})),a=document.createElement('a');a.href=u;a.download=`${state.team}-2021-pass-rush-${visible.length}-plays.csv`;a.click();setTimeout(()=>URL.revokeObjectURL(u),1000);toast(`Exported ${visible.length} filtered plays with source IDs.`);}
